#: passwords.cpp:40
msgid "Echo Characters As"
msgstr "Adleisio Nôdau Fel"

#: passwords.cpp:42
msgid ""
"You can select the type of visual feedback given when you enter a password "
"in kdesu. Choose one of the following options:<p> <ul><li><em>1 star:</em> "
"each character you type is shown as an asterisk (*) symbol.</li> <li><em>3 "
"stars:</em> three asterisks are shown for each character you type.</li> "
"<li><em>no echo:</em> there is no visual feedback at all, so nothing on your "
"screen shows how many characters are in your password.</li></ul>"
msgstr ""
"Gallwch ddewis y math o adborth gweledol y rhoir pan rowch gyfrinair yn "
"kdesu. Dewiswch un o'r dewisiadau canlynol: <p> <ul><li><em> 1 seren:</em> "
"dengys pob nôd y teipiwch fel symbol seren (*).</li> <li><em>3 seren:</em> "
"dengys tair seren am bob nod y teipiwch.</li> <li><em>dim adlais:</em> nid "
"oes adborth gweledol o gwbl, felly nid oes dim ar eich sgrîn i ddangos sawl "
"nôd sydd yn eich cyfrinair.</li></ul>"

#: passwords.cpp:49
msgid "&1 star"
msgstr "&1 seren"

#: passwords.cpp:50
msgid "&3 stars"
msgstr "&3 seren"

#: passwords.cpp:51
msgid "&No echo"
msgstr "&Dim adlais"

#: passwords.cpp:56
msgid "&Remember passwords"
msgstr "&Cofio cyfrineiriau"

#: passwords.cpp:57
msgid ""
"If this option is checked, kdesu will remember your passwords for the "
"specified amount of time. Until then, you won't have to enter your password "
"again. Keep in mind that this option is insecure and may enable others to "
"damage your system.<p> Please <em>do not</em> use this option if you are "
"working in an insecure environment, for example, on a workstation that is "
"located in a publicly accessible area.<p> This option does not affect "
"passwords explicitly set in other applications, for example, your email "
"account password in KMail."
msgstr ""
"Os dewisir y dewis yma, bydd kdesu yn cofio'ch cyfrineiriau am yr amser "
"a benodir. Tan hynny, ni fydd rhaid i chi roi'ch cyfrinair eto. Cofiwch bod y "
"dewisiad yma'n anniogel a gall adael i eraill ddifrodi'ch cysawd.<p> "
"<em>Peidiwch</em> â defnyddio'r dewisiad yma os ydych yn gweithio mewn "
"amgylchedd anniogel, er enghraifft, ar weithfan sydd mewn ardal sy'n agored "
"i'r cyhoedd.<p> Nid oes effaith gan y dewisiad yma ar gyfrineiriau a osodir yn "
"benodol mewn cymhwysiadau eraill, er enghraifft, cyfrinair eich cyfrif ebost yn "
"KMail."

#: passwords.cpp:70
msgid ""
"You can specify how long kdesu will remember your passwords. A short timeout "
"is more secure than a long timeout."
msgstr ""
"Gallwch benodi am gyhyd bydd kdesu yn cofio'ch cyfrineiriau. Mae goramser byr "
"yn fwy diogel na goramser hir."

#: passwords.cpp:73
msgid "&Timeout:"
msgstr "&Goramser:"

#: passwords.cpp:76
msgid " min"
msgstr " mun"

#: passwords.cpp:189
msgid ""
"<h1>Passwords</h1> This module gives you options for configuring the way in "
"which the \"kdesu\" program treats passwords. Kdesu will ask you for a "
"password when you try to carry out some privileged actions, such as changing "
"the date/time stored in your system clock, or adding new users on your "
"computer.<p> You can configure the type of visual feedback given when you "
"type a password, and whether kdesu should remember passwords for some time "
"after you have given them.<p> Note that these settings affect <em>only</em> "
"kdesu. This means that the behavior of passwords in KMail and other programs "
"cannot be configured here."
msgstr ""
"<h1>Cyfrineiriau</h1> Rho'r modwl yma ddewisiadau i chi ffurfweddu'r ffordd "
"mae'r rhaglen \"kdesu\" yn trin cyfrineiriau. Gofynna kdesu i chi am gyfrinair pan "
"geisiwch weithredu rhai gweithredoedd breintiedig, megis newid y dyddiad/amser "
"a gedwir yng nghloc eich cysawd, neu ychwanegu defnyddwyr newydd ar eich "
"cyfrifiadur.<p> Gallwch ffurfweddu'r math o adborth gweledol a roir pan deipiwch "
"gyfrinair, ac a ddylai kdesu gofio cyfrineiriau am gyfnod o amser wedi i chi'u rhoi "
"nhw.<p> Noder bod effaith gan y gosodiadau yma ar kdesu <em>yn unig</em>. "
"Golyga hyn na ellir ffurfweddu ymddygiad cyfrineiriau KMail na rhaglenni eraill yma."

